1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,960
Hey, everybody. Happy Thanksgiving.

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,960
Shh.

3
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:10,000
What, are we keeping Thanksgiving a secret this year?

4
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:12,340
No, we're playing this game I learned at work.

5
00:00:12,550 --> 00:00:15,090
You have to name all the states in six minutes.

6
00:00:15,340 --> 00:00:17,930
What? That's, like, insanely easy.

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:20,720
No, it's harder than it sounds. You always forget at least one.

8
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:24,100
Or in some cases, 14.

9
00:00:25,350 --> 00:00:27,940
It's a stupid game and I wasn't playing against other people...

10
00:00:28,110 --> 00:00:29,860
...so technically, I didn't lose.

11
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,070
You forgot 14 states?

12
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:34,650
Nobody cares about the Dakotas.

13
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:37,490
Oh, okay, time's up.

14
00:00:37,700 --> 00:00:39,070
All right, I got 48.

15
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:40,780
Oh, that's not bad. Pheebs?

16
00:00:40,990 --> 00:00:45,080
Oh, I got tired of naming states, so I decided to list the types of celery.

17
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,250
And I have one, regular celery.

18
00:00:50,340 --> 00:00:54,470
Okay, so Rachel's got 48 and Phoebe has the lead in...

19
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:57,380
...vegetables. Joey?

20
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:00,890
Say hello to the new champ of Chandler's dumb states game.

21
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,100
Wow, how many you got?

22
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,100
Fifty-six.

23
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:48,480
Hey, how is New England not a state?

24
00:01:48,690 --> 00:01:50,850
Huh? They have a sports team.

25
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:53,980
Does South Oregon have a sports team?

26
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,780
There you go.

27
00:01:59,780 --> 00:02:01,780
How come we have one extra place setting?

28
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:06,410
Because you invited your assistant.

29
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:06,410
Oh, right, sorry. Tag's not coming.

30
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:09,500
His girlfriend came into town, so he's spending Thanksgiving with her.

31
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:10,790
Oh, why didn't you tell me?

32
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:14,210
I made him his own individual sweet potato stuffed pumpkin.

33
00:02:14,710 --> 00:02:17,550
Oh, well, I was going to, but then I figured, you know...

34
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:21,010
...your food is so delicious and perfect...

35
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:24,560
...you can never have too many of those pumpkin things.

36
00:02:25,270 --> 00:02:29,850
You'd think I wouldn't enjoy that because it is so fake, ha, ha, but I still do.

37
00:02:31,690 --> 00:02:32,810
Regular celery.

38
00:02:33,060 --> 00:02:34,860
Oh, I already have that.

39
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:40,820
Done, with time to spare.

40
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:45,700
Ooh, this may be a new world's record.

41
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:45,700
You know, I hate to lecture you guys...

42
00:02:45,950 --> 00:02:49,580
...but it's kind of disgraceful that a group of well-educated adults...

43
00:02:49,830 --> 00:02:54,460
...and Joey, can't name all the states.

44
00:02:54,710 --> 00:03:00,090
You ever see a map or one of those round colorful things called a globe?

45
00:03:00,470 --> 00:03:04,340
Uh, Magellan? You got 46 states.

46
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:08,220
What? That's impossible.

47
00:03:04,550 --> 00:03:08,220
Forty-six.

48
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:11,850
Well, who's well-educated now, Mr. I-Forgot-Ten-States?

49
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,940
I'm out of oven space. I'm gonna go turn on Joey's.

50
00:03:16,150 --> 00:03:19,150
Please, watch him. Do not let Joey eat any of the food.

51
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,030
I am only one man.

52
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,870
Okay, time is up.

53
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,870
Give me another minute.

54
00:03:26,030 --> 00:03:29,200
Ross, if you don't know them by now, you will never know them, okay?

55
00:03:29,410 --> 00:03:33,460
That is the beauty of this game. It makes you want to kill yourself.

56
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:35,960
This is crazy. I can do this.

57
00:03:36,210 --> 00:03:39,630
All right, uh, I bet I can get all 50, uh, before dinner.

58
00:03:39,840 --> 00:03:42,090
Okay, but if you can't, no dinner.

59
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,680
You're on.

60
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:47,550
All right, don't look at my list, because there's a lot on there that you don't have.

61
00:03:50,390 --> 00:03:52,390
Hey, did you guys know your oven doesn't work?

62
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:55,480
But the drawer full of takeout menus is okay, right?

63
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:59,480
Ross, I'm gonna use yours, okay?

64
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:59,480
Shh.

65
00:04:00,360 --> 00:04:01,650
Chandler, give me a hand.

66
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:07,070
Sure. Joey, do not let Ross look at any maps or the globe in your apartment.

67
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:10,240
Don't worry, Chandler. It's not a globe of the United States.

68
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:20,590
Hey, you guys, I'm gonna go out and take a walk.

69
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,090
Phoebe, why is your bag moving?

70
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,840
Oh, it's not.

71
00:04:23,300 --> 00:04:25,840
Seriously, it's moving.

72
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:29,550
What the hell's in there?

73
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:29,550
It's just my knitting. That's all.

74
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:37,480
Yes, I knit this.

75
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:40,610
I'm very good.

76
00:04:45,410 --> 00:04:48,450
Ross' apartment is nice. Why don't we hang out here more often?

77
00:04:48,700 --> 00:04:50,450
I don't know. Maybe because it smells weird.

78
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,910
It's like old pumpkins or something.

79
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:56,460
That's my pie.

80
00:04:53,410 --> 00:04:56,460
Which smells delicious.

81
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,960
Uh-oh. Uh-oh.

82
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:58,960
What?

83
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:01,130
We left Joey alone with the food.

84
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:03,590
Yep, yep, I knew it.

85
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,420
There he is...

86
00:05:05,630 --> 00:05:08,760
...feeding stuffing to a dog.

87
00:05:14,480 --> 00:05:17,310
Hi, Geller-Bing residence. How can I help?

88
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:20,110
Phoebe, why is there a dog in our apartment?

89
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:22,110
I'm sorry, who's this?

90
00:05:22,610 --> 00:05:25,320
Phoebe, there's a dog sitting on my couch.

91
00:05:25,530 --> 00:05:28,610
Tell her I'm allergic, and I will sue.

92
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,200
No, there's no dog here.

93
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,200
There is.

94
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:35,580
He's black and white and shaggy.

95
00:05:35,790 --> 00:05:38,170
He's sitting next to Rachel and licking Rachel's hand.

96
00:05:38,370 --> 00:05:40,880
Oh, my God. Where are you?

97
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,300
I'll be right there.

98
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,340
They're here already? How are they doing this?

99
00:05:54,350 --> 00:05:56,600
Hi, Tag. What are you doing here?

100
00:05:56,810 --> 00:06:00,020
I, uh, wanted to see if your offer to spend Thanksgiving with you was still good.

101
00:06:00,230 --> 00:06:02,230
Well, sure. Come in.

102
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:05,110
Well, what happened to your girlfriend?

103
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:07,570
We, uh, kind of broke up this morning.

104
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,200
Oh, I'm sorry.

105
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:11,200
Yeah, so she went back to Ohio.

106
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:14,030
Ohio, thank you.

107
00:06:18,790 --> 00:06:20,210
Huh. Where's the dog?

108
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:22,580
What dog? There's no dog here.

109
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:24,880
Yeah, that dog left.

110
00:06:27,090 --> 00:06:28,420
Phoebe.

111
00:06:28,630 --> 00:06:30,260
Phoebe, open up.

112
00:06:30,550 --> 00:06:31,970
There's no dog in here.

113
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:36,560
Phoebe, we can hear the dog barking.

114
00:06:36,770 --> 00:06:38,390
No, that's just me coughing.

115
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:45,900
Oh, good. There you are.

116
00:06:46,150 --> 00:06:49,190
Listen, um, I have a dog in my room.

117
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,280
What is it doing here?

118
00:06:51,490 --> 00:06:53,780
I'm watching it for friends who went out of town.

119
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,240
Wait.

120
00:06:56,660 --> 00:06:59,410
Hello, my name is Klunkers.

121
00:07:00,210 --> 00:07:02,750
May I please stay with you nice people?

122
00:07:03,540 --> 00:07:07,130
Oh, I wish he could stay here, but Chandler's allergic.

123
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:09,130
Extremely allergic, okay?

124
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:12,550
If I am anywhere near a dog for more than five minutes...

125
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,390
...my throat will just close up.

126
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:19,140
That's odd, because this dog's been living here for the past three days.

127
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:26,520
Really?

128
00:07:28,070 --> 00:07:29,570
If the dog has been here that long...

129
00:07:29,740 --> 00:07:32,570
...and you haven't had a reaction, maybe you're not allergic to this dog.

130
00:07:32,740 --> 00:07:34,950
Well, it still has to go, right?

131
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:36,320
Why?

132
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:40,290
Okay, it's, um...

133
00:07:37,410 --> 00:07:40,290
Don't do it.

134
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:44,250
Don't do what?

135
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:44,250
I have to.

136
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:46,750
Okay? It's time.

137
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,590
Okay, I hate dogs.

138
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:54,760
What?

139
00:07:52,800 --> 00:07:54,760
That's crazy. Why?

140
00:07:56,430 --> 00:07:57,800
Told you.

141
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:04,060
They are needy...

142
00:08:04,270 --> 00:08:07,190
...they are jumpy, and you can't tell what they are thinking...

143
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:09,900
...and that scares me a little bit.

144
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:13,200
You're right. They are scary. Aah!

145
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,780
She just ate a treat out of my hand!

146
00:08:18,450 --> 00:08:22,080
Wait a minute. Do you not like all dogs? I mean, not even puppies?

147
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:23,910
Is there a puppy here?

148
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:28,290
You don't like puppies?

149
00:08:25,460 --> 00:08:28,290
Okay, you are new.

150
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:36,680
Look, Chandler, I told you. Never tell anyone about this dog thing.

151
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:38,850
It's like Ross not liking ice cream.

152
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,730
You don't like ice cream?

153
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,730
It's too cold.

154
00:08:44,850 --> 00:08:47,850
Okay, it's just that dogs make me a little uncomfortable.

155
00:08:48,060 --> 00:08:49,560
Hurts my teeth.

156
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:52,940
I don't wanna say this. I don't want you guys to hate me...

157
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:56,570
...but, uh, I don't think I can be around that dog anymore, okay?

158
00:08:56,820 --> 00:09:00,580
So either the dog goes or I go. Huh.

159
00:09:06,830 --> 00:09:08,750
Oh, my God.

160
00:09:13,090 --> 00:09:14,800
How can I not get this?

161
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:18,550
I'm a college professor. I got 1450 on my SATs.

162
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:20,180
Twelve fifty.

163
00:09:21,350 --> 00:09:23,350
Damn, I forgot you were here.

164
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:26,270
All right. We're gonna take Klunkers to Ross'.

165
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,730
We'll be back in a minute.

166
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,810
Oh, wait, before you go, can I ask a question?

167
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,820
Um, when a guy breaks up with his girlfriend...

168
00:09:33,030 --> 00:09:37,110
...what is an appropriate amount of time to wait before you make a move?

169
00:09:37,320 --> 00:09:38,990
Oh, I'd say about a month.

170
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,410
Really? I'd say three to four.

171
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:42,410
Half-hour.

172
00:09:46,710 --> 00:09:48,160
Interesting.

173
00:09:48,870 --> 00:09:50,830
When it's your assistant, I would say never.

174
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,630
All right, Rach, the big question is, does he like you?

175
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:58,800
Right? Because if he doesn't like you, this is all a moo point.

176
00:10:00,050 --> 00:10:03,180
Huh. A "moo" point?

177
00:10:05,220 --> 00:10:08,180
Yeah. It's like a cow's opinion.

178
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:11,730
It just doesn't matter.

179
00:10:14,320 --> 00:10:15,690
It's "moo."

180
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:25,700
Have I been living with him for too long, or did that all just make sense?

181
00:10:26,830 --> 00:10:29,960
Please don't listen to Joey. Okay? Would you look at him?

182
00:10:30,170 --> 00:10:32,920
He's obviously depressed. He's away from his family.

183
00:10:33,170 --> 00:10:34,790
He's spending Thanksgiving with strangers.

184
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,090
What he needs right now is for you to be his friend.

185
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:39,880
Oh, you're right. I'm sorry. Thank you.

186
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:44,050
Okay, that's what I'm going to do.

187
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:44,050
Fine, take their advice.

188
00:10:44,310 --> 00:10:45,760
No one ever listens to me.

189
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:49,480
When the package is this pretty, no one cares what's inside.

190
00:10:55,570 --> 00:10:57,690
Hey.

191
00:10:55,570 --> 00:10:57,690
Hey.

192
00:10:57,900 --> 00:10:59,490
How you holding up?

193
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,400
Not bad.

194
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:01,400
Yeah?

195
00:11:01,610 --> 00:11:04,910
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

196
00:11:01,610 --> 00:11:04,910
Thanks.

197
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:09,370
Were you guys together a long time?

198
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:09,370
A year, on and off.

199
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:13,040
I thought we'd end up together. I don't anymore.

200
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:15,750
Now that she broke up with you.

201
00:11:13,250 --> 00:11:15,750
Yeah.

202
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,670
Hmm.

203
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,670
It's weird.

204
00:11:18,880 --> 00:11:23,300
I always used to assume that I would meet someone and fall in love and be happy.

205
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:27,600
That all that was just a given. Well, lately, it's like, what if it's not?

206
00:11:28,270 --> 00:11:30,100
Do you ever have that feeling?

207
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:31,810
No.

208
00:11:32,310 --> 00:11:33,480
Yeah.

209
00:11:34,360 --> 00:11:36,820
All the time. Constantly. It's terrifying.

210
00:11:37,070 --> 00:11:40,320
But, you know, then I figure it has to work out.

211
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,320
Why?

212
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:45,160
Because it has to.

213
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:49,950
You have all the answers, don't you?

214
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:49,950
Yeah, I know, I do. I really do.

215
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:54,790
Hey, thanks for talking to me.

216
00:11:51,160 --> 00:11:54,790
Come on, what are bosses for?

217
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:56,420
Hug it out.

218
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,130
All right, he likes you back.

219
00:12:01,420 --> 00:12:05,180
Huh? Told you you should go for it.

220
00:12:06,430 --> 00:12:07,800
What?

221
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:13,390
Street noise drown any of that out?

222
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:17,480
No? All right, I'll see you later. Ha, ha. Okay.

223
00:12:22,030 --> 00:12:24,820
What did Joey say? I like you back?

224
00:12:24,990 --> 00:12:27,700
Uh, yeah... You know, well, see, he...

225
00:12:28,740 --> 00:12:33,710
Joey knows that I'm very insecure about my back.

226
00:12:33,960 --> 00:12:37,210
And... And you were hugging me...

227
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:41,590
...so obviously you are not repulsed by it. Yeah. Heh.

228
00:12:43,380 --> 00:12:45,130
Wait a minute, that doesn't make any sense.

229
00:12:45,300 --> 00:12:46,380
No?

230
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:52,560
All right, here's the truth. Ahem.

231
00:12:52,730 --> 00:12:55,770
Joey said what he said because, um...

232
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,310
...I'm attracted to you.

233
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,490
Wow.

234
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,490
Yeah, I admit it.

235
00:13:03,860 --> 00:13:08,910
I have a crush on you. And, uh, I know that's crazy because we work together...

236
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,870
...and nothing could ever happen.

237
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,500
And the last thing I wanted to do was freak you out...

238
00:13:13,700 --> 00:13:16,660
...or make you feel uncomfortable.

239
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:21,420
Which is why it would be really great if you said something right about now.

240
00:13:22,340 --> 00:13:25,260
Oh, my God. Those guys are stealing my car.

241
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:28,260
What?

242
00:13:25,420 --> 00:13:28,260
Right there. That's my car.

243
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,640
Hey!

244
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,640
Okay, that's gonna take a minute.

245
00:13:31,810 --> 00:13:34,430
Do you have anything else you wanna get off your chest?

246
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,980
I can't believe this.

247
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:39,900
Wait, we still have time to talk, and they're not even in the car yet.

248
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:42,070
Oh, look, there they go. Okay.

249
00:13:43,650 --> 00:13:46,440
Okay, Phoebe. We should probably go back now.

250
00:13:46,950 --> 00:13:49,360
Please, don't leave me. I'll be lonely.

251
00:13:50,370 --> 00:13:52,490
Stop it. Stop.

252
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:56,450
Okay, let's go. We can be strong.

253
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:56,450
Yeah, okay.

254
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:02,460
Oh, my God, did you hear that? She said "Monica."

255
00:14:03,420 --> 00:14:06,050
Oh, I can't leave her.

256
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:09,340
If you want, we could sneak the dog back in and Chandler wouldn't even know.

257
00:14:09,510 --> 00:14:10,590
That's not gonna work.

258
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:13,970
I had that dog there for three days and Chandler had no idea.

259
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:15,600
He's not so smart.

260
00:14:15,810 --> 00:14:18,390
Hey. I didn't know either.

261
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:22,940
Yeah, but you kind of knew that something was going on, didn't you?

262
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,900
Yeah, I knew. Heh.

263
00:14:31,030 --> 00:14:32,070
Where's Chandler?

264
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,910
Here I am.

265
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:35,910
Wash your hands.

266
00:14:38,330 --> 00:14:39,870
How did you know?

267
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:46,090
Hey, what's she doing back here?

268
00:14:46,300 --> 00:14:49,220
Relax, Ross. She's not made of ice cream.

269
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:54,260
Hey, look, Phoebe. I, uh, laid out the states geographically.

270
00:14:54,430 --> 00:14:55,850
No, no, we don't have time for this.

271
00:14:56,020 --> 00:14:57,810
We have to keep Chandler away from my room.

272
00:14:57,980 --> 00:14:59,140
Yeah, but, look what I...

273
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:01,940
See, this is exactly what we do not have time for.

274
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:09,860
Where's Monica?

275
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:09,860
Uh, in Phoebe's room. You can't go in.

276
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:11,320
Why not?

277
00:15:13,990 --> 00:15:15,830
Monica's crying.

278
00:15:17,370 --> 00:15:21,160
She's very upset about this whole Klunkers thing.

279
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:24,500
Well, I should go in there.

280
00:15:21,370 --> 00:15:24,500
No, no.

281
00:15:24,670 --> 00:15:28,210
No, she doesn't want to see you right now.

282
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:32,380
Why not?

283
00:15:29,550 --> 00:15:32,380
Because you sent away the dog.

284
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,890
That's ridiculous.

285
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,890
Oh, is it? Is it?

286
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:42,690
Look, when Monica and I were kids, we had a dog named Rover.

287
00:15:42,940 --> 00:15:46,770
And, um, one day, my dad decides he doesn't like dogs.

288
00:15:46,980 --> 00:15:50,940
So Monica and her friend... Phyllis...

289
00:15:52,150 --> 00:15:55,280
...take away the dog, and that was the last time we ever saw him.

290
00:15:55,450 --> 00:15:58,950
Don't you see? This is just like that...

291
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:03,000
...only with a few details changed.

292
00:16:06,420 --> 00:16:08,590
Okay, I'm in my sweatpants.

293
00:16:08,840 --> 00:16:10,130
Bring on the food.

294
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:16,140
What's the matter?

295
00:16:13,930 --> 00:16:16,140
Monica's all upset...

296
00:16:16,300 --> 00:16:18,680
...because I sent Klunkers away.

297
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:21,100
So? Bring the dog back. You're a hero.

298
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:25,060
Yeah, I could be a hero. I could do that. I could... I could do...

299
00:16:25,310 --> 00:16:27,520
What if it...? What if it attacks me?

300
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,780
Chandler, it's like a big gerbil.

301
00:16:32,860 --> 00:16:35,070
And that doesn't scare you?

302
00:16:40,120 --> 00:16:41,830
Ross, you need some help?

303
00:16:42,290 --> 00:16:43,330
From you?

304
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:46,620
Yes, please.

305
00:16:52,340 --> 00:16:54,550
First of all, Utah?

306
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:57,470
Dude, you can't just make stuff up.

307
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:06,190
I hate America.

308
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:09,940
When I finish this game, I swear I am moving.

309
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:15,150
Hey. Tag still talking to the police?

310
00:17:12,190 --> 00:17:15,150
Yeah.

311
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,910
Ugh, damn it. Why did I open my mouth?

312
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:20,830
"I have a crush on you. I'm attracted to you."

313
00:17:21,080 --> 00:17:23,200
I know that I freaked him out.

314
00:17:23,410 --> 00:17:26,000
If you said it like that, you probably did, yeah.

315
00:17:28,330 --> 00:17:29,540
Hey, is Chandler here?

316
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:32,130
Uh, no, no, he went for a walk.

317
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:34,800
Okay, well, you cannot tell him, but look who's back.

318
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:39,260
Hi.

319
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:39,260
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

320
00:17:39,430 --> 00:17:41,890
He went over to Ross' to bring the dog back here.

321
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:44,890
Oh, no, the dog's not going to be there.

322
00:17:46,850 --> 00:17:47,890
You think?

323
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,440
Hi, honey.

324
00:17:53,860 --> 00:17:56,690
Please, please, please, don't be mad at me.

325
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,860
What? Why would...?

326
00:17:56,900 --> 00:17:58,860
Shh. Wait and see.

327
00:17:59,070 --> 00:18:01,370
Maybe we will, maybe we won't.

328
00:18:02,490 --> 00:18:06,080
Okay, I went over to Ross' apartment to bring back Klunkers, you know, for you...

329
00:18:06,250 --> 00:18:10,830
...and, ahem, I left the door open, and she must've gotten out.

330
00:18:11,380 --> 00:18:15,590
And I looked everywhere, all over the apartment, including the roof.

331
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:19,760
Which, FYI, Ross, one of your neighbors, growing weed.

332
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,050
I couldn't find him...

333
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:27,230
...and I am so, so, so sorry.

334
00:18:27,480 --> 00:18:32,020
But I do know where we can all go ease the pain.

335
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,820
We have good news. Look who's back.

336
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,570
Hi.

337
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:40,820
Klunkers. Oh, my God.

338
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:46,620
That's right. She came back all by herself.

339
00:18:40,990 --> 00:18:46,620
It's a Thanksgiving miracle.

340
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,870
It is so good to see you.

341
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:53,210
Yeah, she came all the way back from Ross' building.

342
00:18:53,460 --> 00:18:56,170
Oh, the things she must've seen.

343
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:58,550
Then she climbed up the fire escape...

344
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:01,430
...and she tapped on the window with her teeny little paw...

345
00:19:01,590 --> 00:19:03,510
...and we ran to let her in.

346
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:07,270
I went too far, didn't I?

347
00:19:08,180 --> 00:19:10,180
When should I have stopped?

348
00:19:15,270 --> 00:19:20,110
Okay, maybe this is so hard because there aren't 50 states.

349
00:19:21,990 --> 00:19:25,410
Let me tell you something. I have 49 states.

350
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:27,700
Now, there are no more.

351
00:19:29,040 --> 00:19:32,000
Now, I think I should be able to eat something.

352
00:19:33,170 --> 00:19:34,210
It's up to you.

353
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,880
Oh, hi. How are you doing?

354
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:41,880
I'm okay.

355
00:19:42,090 --> 00:19:45,090
I gotta go down to the police station and look at mug shots.

356
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:49,430
Thanks for having me over, you guys.

357
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:49,430
Tag, you're going? Uh...

358
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,020
We didn't, uh, get a chance to talk.

359
00:19:52,270 --> 00:19:54,650
So where did you say you're from again?

360
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,320
Colorado.

361
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,320
Ah, what good are you?

362
00:20:03,610 --> 00:20:07,490
Look, um, I think we should talk about what happened on the terrace.

363
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,080
Okay.

364
00:20:07,700 --> 00:20:09,080
Uh...

365
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:11,000
I never should've said what I said.

366
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:13,210
You know what? It just doesn't matter how I feel.

367
00:20:13,370 --> 00:20:17,460
We work together, so nothing could really ever happen between us.

368
00:20:17,710 --> 00:20:22,590
What I would love is just to go to work on Monday and never talk about this again.

369
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:25,260
Okay? Big day, Monday. Lots to do.

370
00:20:26,970 --> 00:20:28,300
So we okay?

371
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:30,680
Um, I'm not.

372
00:20:30,890 --> 00:20:34,230
Oh, God, I knew it. I freaked you out.

373
00:20:30,890 --> 00:20:34,230
No, you didn't.

374
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,600
The only thing that freaked me out was you saying...

375
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:38,690
...that nothing could happen between us.

376
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:42,030
Really?

377
00:20:39,730 --> 00:20:42,030
Yeah.

378
00:20:42,650 --> 00:20:45,400
So please don't fire me for doing this.

379
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,670
Okay, well, that's one less thing we have to do on Monday.

380
00:21:20,270 --> 00:21:21,650
Delaware.

381
00:21:25,360 --> 00:21:26,860
Delaware.

382
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:30,620
All right.

383
00:21:27,530 --> 00:21:30,620
I want my turkey now.

384
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:32,700
You got it.

385
00:21:37,790 --> 00:21:40,000
You got Nevada twice.

386
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,460
I know.

387
00:21:43,420 --> 00:21:44,460
Yeah.

